		<dict>
			<key>FooterText</key>
			<string>A style sets the capitals, the punctuation and the words: Formal. keeps every mark; Excited! ends short sentences with “!”; Casual drops the last period and the comma after “so” or “hey”; very casual is Casual in lowercase; texting also writes btw, u and tn; slang also writes fr and fire. Each app can have its own in the iikb app. Where a style keeps capitals, they follow Auto-Capitalization in Typing. As Said types every word you say, um and uh too; No Um or Uh leaves those out; Clean also leaves out words said twice, “like” and “you know” said between commas, what you take back with “scratch that”, and what you fix as you go (“two, I mean three”).</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Writing</string>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSGroupSpecifier</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>DefaultValue</key>
			<string>casual</string>
			<key>Key</key>
			<string>writingStyle</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Style</string>
			<key>Titles</key>
			<array>
				<string>Formal.</string>
				<string>Excited!</string>
				<string>Casual</string>
				<string>very casual</string>
				<string>texting</string>
				<string>slang</string>
			</array>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSMultiValueSpecifier</string>
			<key>Values</key>
			<array>
				<string>formal</string>
				<string>excited</string>
				<string>casual</string>
				<string>veryCasual</string>
				<string>texting</string>
